host.setup on box, resume
 1 packages: install ca-certificates, curl, gnupg, ufw, fail2ban, unattended-upgrades, jq, git (missing ca-certificates, curl, gnupg, ufw, fail2ban, unattended-upgrades, jq, git)
 2 hostname: set the hostname to box (currently personal-vps)
 3 timezone: set the timezone to UTC (currently Etc/UTC)
 4 swap: keep a 4 GiB swap file (already 4.0 GiB)
 5 docker: install Docker from Docker's repository, with compose and buildx (not installed)
 6 registry: run the local image registry on 127.0.0.1:5000 (already running)
 7 cloudflare-ranges: keep Cloudflare's address ranges at /etc/bedrock/cloudflare-ranges.json, which the edge trusts to name visitors behind its proxy (read from Cloudflare)
 8 edge: run the web edge on ports 80 and 443 (already running)
 9 security-updates: install security updates automatically, without automatic reboots (already on)
10 journal: cap the system journal at 1G for 14 days (already capped)
11 ssh: allow only key logins over SSH (already keys only)
12 firewall: allow ssh in, and 80 and 443 only from Cloudflare, Docker's published ports included (the web is open to anyone)
13 fail2ban: ban repeated SSH failures (already active)
14 pushes: keep the bedrock user, which receives git pushes; each of its keys deploys only the apps it names (no bedrock user yet)
15 time: keep the clock synchronized (already synchronized)
16 profile: record the profile at /etc/bedrock/host.json
